# 5. Morse encoder

Create a separate encoder:

```kotlin
class MorseEncoder {

    fun encode(text: String): String {
        return text
            .uppercase()
            .trim()
            .split(Regex("\\s+"))
            .joinToString(" / ") { word ->
                word.mapNotNull { MorseDictionary.codes[it] }
                    .joinToString(" ")
            }
    }
}
```

Example:

```kotlin
MorseEncoder().encode("SOS")
```

returns:

```text
... --- ...
```

And:

```kotlin
MorseEncoder().encode("HELLO WORLD")
```

returns:

```text
.... . .-.. .-.. --- / .-- --- .-. .-.. -..
```

The `/` represents a word boundary.

